+---
+description: Methodology garbage-collection — the exhaust leg of the capture pipeline. Retires promoted memories, flags §1 rule-family consolidation, sweeps stale/orphaned memory entries, and reports budget health for the always-on surfaces.
+---
+
+# /gc — methodology garbage-collection
+
+You are running the **methodology-GC** protocol. The user invoked `/gc $ARGUMENTS`.
+
+**Premise:** the methodology has world-class *capture* (triage → memory → `/codify` → keeper) and this command is its *exhaust*. Without GC, always-on surfaces grow monotonically: `MEMORY.md` gets harness-truncated (silent recall loss), CLAUDE.md §1 outgrows what a session can apply, and promoted rules keep loading twice. Origin: the 2026-07 harness audit (MEMORY.md 419 lines → 55% truncated including Active Project Decisions; 20/20 sampled §1 rules double-indexed). → `KB § PATTERNS/common/methodology-gc.md`
+
+**Cadence:** monthly, or immediately when `check_memory_md_index` / the router rule-count budget warns.
+
+## Protocol
+
+1. **Measure budgets** — report each vs. its ceiling:
+   - `MEMORY.md`: lines (ceiling 200) + bytes (ceiling 20KB) + lines >200 chars (ceiling 0).
+   - CLAUDE.md §1: `- **` rule count (target 50; keeper `check_claude_md_router` hard-caps at 55).
+   - `KNOWLEDGE-BASE/CONTEXT/PATTERNS/common/`: file count (junk-drawer threshold 50 — propose a topical split above it).
+2. **Retire promoted memories** — for each MEMORY.md index entry whose rule now lives in CLAUDE.md §1, a `CLAUDE/<topic>.md`, or a keeper: move the index line to `memory/ARCHIVE-INDEX.md` (same directory as `MEMORY.md`). NEVER delete the body file — vector recall still reaches it (learn-before-archive).
+3. **Sweep stale sections** — `Completed`, `Checkpoints`, and any `Active Project Decisions` entry older than 3 months: verify against the codebase/git (codebase is source of truth), then archive the resolved ones the same way. Re-order what remains: **Active Project Decisions and open items go ABOVE the long tail** — harness truncation is positional; the top of the file is the part guaranteed to load.
+4. **Sweep orphans** — memory files absent from both `MEMORY.md` and `ARCHIVE-INDEX.md`: index the live ones, archive the superseded ones. (`ls memory/*.md` vs. grep of both indexes.)
+5. **Flag §1 consolidation candidates** — ≥4 §1 rules sharing one family (cache, branching/dispatch, …) ⇒ propose collapsing to a single family line pointing at a KB family-index doc. Propose only; §1 edits are router surgery — apply with user consent, keeper-gated.
+6. **Report** — budgets before/after, entries retired/archived/re-indexed, consolidation proposals. If everything is within budget: say so and stop — a no-op GC is a healthy result.
+
+## Guardrails
+- **Learn-before-archive is absolute** — GC moves *index lines*, never deletes *body files*. `ARCHIVE-INDEX.md` preserves every retired line (name + hook), so nothing is unfindable.
+- Verify before archiving a "stale" project decision — docs drift; the tree wins. An entry that looks stale but reflects live state gets a refreshed hook instead of the archive.
+- §1 and keeper changes ride the normal gates (`check_claude_md_router`, kb_sync) — never `--no-verify`.
+- GC is not `/codify` — it retires and consolidates what's already decided; it never promotes new rules. If step 2 surfaces an unpromoted ripe candidate, hand it to `/codify`.
+
+Reference: `KB § PATTERNS/common/methodology-gc.md` · `KB § PATTERNS/common/methodology-codification-pipeline.md` (this command closes its loop) · `KB § PATTERNS/common/persistent-files-absorption.md`.
