+## 7 · KB-autostage hook hazard — why engineers never commit + the architect's scoped-commit recipe
+
+(Moved here 2026-07-14 from `engineer-seed.md §2` — the agent file keeps the rule + pointer; this section is the canonical depth.)
+
+`scripts/hooks/pre-commit` (CLAUDE.md §4 sync rule) runs `git add` on *every* modified `KNOWLEDGE-BASE/**`, `CLAUDE.md`, `CLAUDE/*.md`, `INDEX.md`, and `PROJECT-HISTORY.md` on every commit. In a multi-agent dirty tree this means a pathspec / "scoped" `git commit <paths>` is **NOT actually scoped** — it silently absorbs other agents' unstaged KB/doc work under your message (commit-only-your-own-work violation).
+
+Consequences:
+- **(a) Engineers never `git commit`** — architect-only, no exceptions. This is the structural reason behind the engineer stage-only contract, not a trust judgment.
+- **(b) The architect**, committing a scoped change while the tree is dirty, MUST either `git commit --no-verify <explicit paths>` with the bypass rationale written into the commit message, **or** commit from a clean tree — and MUST always verify `git show --stat HEAD` immediately after. Surprise files ⇒ `git reset --soft HEAD^` recover (local/unpushed = zero loss) + re-commit scoped. The KB docs' own sync is verified when the proper consolidation commit lands them.
+
+**Recurrence 2026-05-17** (`cc9e69b`): a 2-file conftest commit swept 7 unrelated KB docs including another agent's unreviewed edit; soft-reset-recovered → re-committed as `7137af0`. This incident is why the recipe above exists.
+
+This section is also the named home of the architect-side `--no-verify` carve-out referenced throughout this doc ("the `engineer-seed.md §2` KB-autostage-hook carve-out shape") — the ONE legitimate `--no-verify` use, always with the rationale in the commit message.
