+# Methodology GC — retirement as a first-class leg
+
+> **Rule:** every capture pipeline needs an exhaust. Promotion to an always-on surface (CLAUDE.md §1 · keeper · `CLAUDE/<topic>.md`) RETIRES the memory index line that spawned it, same commit; `/gc` sweeps the strays on a monthly cadence and keeps the always-on surfaces inside their budgets.
+
+## Why this exists (2026-07 harness audit)
+
+The methodology accumulated capture mechanisms for years — triage, auto-memory, `/codify`, auto-improvement ledger, keepers — and zero decay mechanisms. Measured consequences:
+
+- `MEMORY.md` reached 419 lines / 56KB; the harness truncates on load, so **~55% of the index (including `Active Project Decisions`) was silently invisible every session**. Truncation is positional — the stalest content (top) loaded, the operationally current tail didn't.
+- **20/20 sampled CLAUDE.md §1 rules were still also indexed in MEMORY.md** — every promoted rule paid context twice, forever (promotion-without-retirement).
+- §1 grew to 72 always-on rules; `PATTERNS/common/` to 73 files. Both keepers were green — they gate *shape*, not *growth*.
+
+The general lesson: **a green gate on shape does not bound accumulation.** Growth needs its own budget + its own exhaust.
+
+## The mechanism (two legs, gate-methodology-sync compliant)
+
+1. **By-construction leg** — `/codify` step 6 ends with retirement: the promoted entry's `MEMORY.md` line moves to `memory/ARCHIVE-INDEX.md` (body file untouched — vector recall still reaches it).
+2. **Backstop leg** — `/gc` (`.claude/commands/gc.md`): budget measurement (MEMORY.md ≤200 lines / ≤20KB target, keeper caps 40KB; §1 target 50 rules, keeper caps 55; `common/` ≤50 files), stray-promotion retirement, stale-section sweep, orphan re-indexing, §1 family-consolidation proposals. Keeper `check_memory_md_index` (advisory) fires the cadence.
+
+## Invariants
+
+- **Learn-before-archive:** GC moves index lines, never deletes body files. `ARCHIVE-INDEX.md` preserves every retired line.
+- **Positional loading:** `MEMORY.md` orders active/open content first; archives and long-tail reference live at the bottom or out of the file entirely.
+- **Verify-then-archive:** an entry is retired because the tree proves it resolved/promoted — never because it *looks* old.
+- **GC ≠ codify:** GC never promotes; ripe candidates surfaced mid-sweep route to `/codify`.
+
+## Consumers
+
+`/gc` · `/codify` (step 6 retirement) · `check_memory_md_index` (advisory keeper) · the auto-memory writing discipline (new entries go above the long tail, one line, <200 chars).
